== C. no usage baseline exists for a trend ==
`previousRetroTotalTokens` selects the highest-numbered retro below 32 — retro-28 —
and greps it for "Total tokens:". Measured: retro-28 has NO ## Usage section, so the
trend line will read "no prior retro found for comparison".
Audited all 9 retros on record: 6 carry no Usage section at all —
  retro-4b, retro-23, retro-25, retro-26, retro-27, retro-28
Only retro-5, retro-6 and retro-7 have one. D-013 has required it since 2026-09-19.
By my own lex §7 an absent usage section on a real cascade is "the Censor's own gap,
not the tool's" — so this is a standing lapse of my own contract, named here rather
than quietly skipped. Cascade 32 restores it; 29-31 are unfiled and are the
orchestrator's call (backfill or recorded skip), not mine to take.

