== E. a defect in my own evidence practice ==
studio/ci/W-065-review-1.log and -2.log both cite the mutation battery as "Scripts
kept: $TMPDIR/mut/mutate{,2,3,4}.py". $TMPDIR is session-scoped and will not survive
this session, so that citation degrades to a dead reference the moment the session
ends — while the logs that cite it are committed to the officina forever.
The standing rule is "mechanical work is a script you write, run and keep". I wrote
and ran them; "keep" is where I fell short. Naming it rather than letting a
committed log carry a path that resolves to nothing.

